body:
> So the marshaller returning back string for all other formats is expected isn't it?

@admad The `@return` annotation is `\Cake\I18n\Time|\DateTime`. So no one would expect it returns strings. I was surprised when I got a fatal error  from the following code:
```php
if ($this->Articles->save($article)) {
    $article->published->format('Y-m-d H:i:s');
}
```
If it is a feature, I would hesitate to use the `DateTimeType` class.

What is the benefit of returning strings? I cannot see any good reasons.
